  "qualification": "Local owner, source-preservation, execution and headless interaction checks, plus four directly viewed offscreen normal-host frames. No native Access/Windows interaction, complete QueryDef lifecycle or full Access SQL conformance claim.",
  "observations": [
    "SQL tokenizer/name rules own QBE Alias: operand prefixes; colons inside quoted names, strings and dates are not split. Executable SELECT grammar is unchanged. Builder field editing retains explicit source identity and treats arbitrary expressions separately.",
    "Every accepted raw edit advances the draft revision. Incomplete syntax survives blur, another-column editing, object parking and fresh-source preferences; Build, Run, SQL publication, import and stale consuming actions cannot execute the older parsed model.",
    "Hard byte, parser nesting/token and allocation refusals preserve the whole previous candidate. Real Field Paste tests exercise independent nesting/token limits below the text-byte allowance and observe unchanged draft/request/raw text/prior rows with no emitted action.",
    "Raw text, immutable Cancel baseline and current parsed payload share the explicit editable reservation; retained-memory accounting includes immutable owners and actual capacities. Cancel restores only that field and adjusts available authoring bytes.",
    "Focused Field Escape uses the actual TextEdit filter plus exact previous-frame ownership to survive repeated accessibility focus requests. Popup Escape is separate; a subsequent Escape without retained input releases focus normally.",
    "Tab close, Ctrl+W, destructive user Open/Create/Exit and updater restart preserve unresolved active or parked text. This is a temporary finish-or-explicit-Cancel editor restriction, not native dirty-query Save/Save As parity. Current scratch SQL is singleton per document; no unreachable two-scratch-tab test was fabricated.",
    "Actual native cell save, consuming acknowledgment and guarded fresh reopen preserve parked raw text/tab identity while dropping stale result/native capabilities. User file-dialog/queued opens remain guarded before selected-path/password consumption.",
    "Actual Runtime and MCP Build/Run retain aliases and typed source identities without changing native source bytes. All eight sectioned Fluent catalogs pass their current key/variable/format checks in the selected UI run."
  ],
